In this example, with |Ey| and phase(Ey) components, convergence to decent optimum
is reasonably straightforward. Similar behaviour to legacy kernel

# See data
csem1Dplotter data

# smoothing style
csem1Dinverter -v 2 -q --NS --LM -s -P --startup startup

# raw unsmoothed case
csem1Dinverter -v 2 -q --NS --LM -P --no-smoothing-weights --startup startup

# splitting
csem1Dinverter -v 2 -q --NS --LM -P --auto-split --MS d --startup startup | grep Gridding:

# Plot profiles, or solutions
csem1Dplotter resp_final

graph -TX profile_final.txt
